{
  "summary": "This experiment tested replacing the ResNet50 image encoder with ImageNet ViT-L in a multimodal setup using multiprofile data, scvi_n200 RNA encoder, avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion. Validation accuracy improved to 0.7150 (F1: 0.6872), higher than the prior multimodal baseline (0.6315). The result suggests the image encoder choice may influence performance, but the exact contribution of this change versus other design factors remains uncertain without direct comparison to alternative encoders in the same configuration."
}

